---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Self-host — moved (PM 1.2.0)">
  <section style="padding: 3rem 0 2rem;">
    <h1>Self-host is no longer a separate thing</h1>
    <p style="max-width: 40rem; color: #4d4d4d;">
      PM v1.2.0 runs directly against <strong>your Anthropic account</strong> — there is no
      PM-operated backend to self-host around. Bring your own Anthropic API key, everything
      else is local.
    </p>
    <pre><code>npm install -g @sinameraji/pm

cd your-product-repo
pm init       # paste your Anthropic API key
pm audit</code></pre>
    <p style="max-width: 40rem;">
      Your key is stored in <code>~/.pm/config.yaml</code> (chmod 600) and only ever sent to
      <code>api.anthropic.com</code>. No markup on inference. Your rate limits, your bill.
    </p>
    <p style="max-width: 40rem;">
      Coming from PM 1.1.x with a self-hosted Cloudflare Worker? Take it down — it's no longer
      referenced. See
      <a href="https://github.com/sinameraji/tpm/blob/main/docs/migration-from-1.1.md">the
      migration notes</a>.
    </p>
    <p style="max-width: 40rem; margin-top: 2rem;">
      <a href="/" class="button">Back to PM</a>
      <a href="/docs" class="button secondary" style="margin-left: 0.5rem;">Docs</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
